          "text": "{\"items\":[{\"rank\":1,\"display_phrase\":\"by default\",\"source_span\":\"by default\",\"source_sentence\":\"During those hours, apps covered by the plan would be unavailable by default.\",\"ja_gloss\":\"初期設定で\",\"phrase_type\":\"prepositional_phrase\",\"normalization_type\":\"none\",\"normalization_note\":\"本文どおりの定型表現。\",\"selection_reason\":\"規制が強制ではなく初期設定として働くという、記事全体の中心的な仕組みを理解する鍵。\",\"listening_difficulty_reason\":\"弱く速く発音されやすい短い機能語の連続で、音声では聞き落としやすい。\",\"inference_transparency\":\"MEDIUM\",\"topic_exposure_dependency\":\"MEDIUM\",\"comprehension_impact\":\"HIGH\",\"figurative_or_emotional_value\":\"LOW\",\"spoiler_risk\":\"LOW\",\"portfolio_category\":\"compact_listening_pattern\",\"portfolio_substitution\":false,\"portfolio_substitution_reason\":\"該当なし。各カテゴリから2件ずつ選定。\"},{\"rank\":2,\"display_phrase\":\"opt out\",\"source_span\":\"opt out\",\"source_sentence\":\"Teenagers aged 16 and 17 would still be able to change the settings and opt out.\",\"ja_gloss\":\"適用を拒否する\",\"phrase_type\":\"phrasal_verb\",\"normalization_type\":\"none\",\"normalization_note\":\"本文ですでに動詞の基本形。\",\"selection_reason\":\"利用者が規制を解除できるという重要な例外を表す句動詞。\",\"listening_difficulty_reason\":\"二つの短い語が連結しやすく、outを聞き逃すと「変更可能」という意味を把握できない。\",\"inference_transparency\":\"MEDIUM\",\"topic_exposure_dependency\":\"MEDIUM\",\"comprehension_impact\":\"HIGH\",\"figurative_or_emotional_value\":\"LOW\",\"spoiler_risk\":\"LOW\",\"portfolio_category\":\"compact_listening_pattern\",\"portfolio_substitution\":false,\"portfolio_substitution_reason\":\"該当なし。各カテゴリから2件ずつ選定。\"},{\"rank\":3,\"display_phrase\":\"digital switch-off period\",\"source_span\":\"digital switch-off period\",\"source_sentence\":\"On July 15, the British government announced plans for a digital switch-off period for 16- and 17-year-olds.\",\"ja_gloss\":\"デジタル利用停止時間帯\",\"phrase_type\":\"technical_term\",\"normalization_type\":\"none\",\"normalization_note\":\"政策を指す複合名詞をそのまま見出し化。\",\"selection_reason\":\"英国の計画そのものを指す題材固有の中心語で、対象となる措置の全体像を支える。\",\"listening_difficulty_reason\":\"三語が一まとまりの複合名詞として発音され、switch-offを動詞と誤認しやすい。\",\"inference_transparency\":\"HIGH\",\"topic_exposure_dependency\":\"HIGH\",\"comprehension_impact\":\"HIGH\",\"figurative_or_emotional_value\":\"MEDIUM\",\"spoiler_risk\":\"MEDIUM\",\"portfolio_category\":\"domain_expression\",\"portfolio_substitution\":false,\"portfolio_substitution_reason\":\"該当なし。各カテゴリから2件ずつ選定。\"},{\"rank\":4,\"display_phrase\":\"personalized recommendation feed\",\"source_span\":\"Personalized recommendation feeds\",\"source_sentence\":\"Personalized recommendation feeds would also be turned off.\",\"ja_gloss\":\"個人向けおすすめフィード\",\"phrase_type\":\"technical_term\",\"normalization_type\":\"noun_canonical\",\"normalization_note\":\"本文の複数形feedsを単数の見出し形feedに変更。\",\"selection_reason\":\"夜間に停止される主要機能の一つで、スクロールを促す仕組みの理解に必要。\",\"listening_difficulty_reason\":\"長い修飾語personalizedとrecommendationが連続し、名詞の中心であるfeedまで保持しにくい。\",\"inference_transparency\":\"MEDIUM\",\"topic_exposure_dependency\":\"HIGH\",\"comprehension_impact\":\"HIGH\",\"figurative_or_emotional_value\":\"LOW\",\"spoiler_risk\":\"MEDIUM\",\"portfolio_category\":\"domain_expression\",\"portfolio_substitution\":false,\"portfolio_substitution_reason\":\"該当なし。各カテゴリから2件ずつ選定。\"},{\"rank\":5,\"display_phrase\":\"speed bump\",\"source_span\":\"speed bump\",\"source_sentence\":\"In other words, the plan puts a small speed bump before the automatic urge to watch “just one more.”\",\"ja_gloss\":\"小さな心理的障害\",\"phrase_type\":\"noun_phrase\",\"normalization_type\":\"none\",\"normalization_note\":\"比喩の核となる二語だけを抽出。\",\"selection_reason\":\"完全な禁止ではなく、一度立ち止まらせる仕組みだという政策の狙いを視覚的に表す中心比喩。\",\"listening_difficulty_reason\":\"通常は道路の減速帯を指すため、設定変更の手間を表す比喩へ即座に切り替える必要がある。\",\"inference_transparency\":\"MEDIUM\",\"topic_exposure_dependency\":\"LOW\",\"comprehension_impact\":\"HIGH\",\"figurative_or_emotional_value\":\"HIGH\",\"spoiler_risk\":\"LOW\",\"portfolio_category\":\"figurative_emotional\",\"portfolio_substitution\":false,\"portfolio_substitution_reason\":\"該当なし。各カテゴリから2件ずつ選定。\"},{\"rank\":6,\"display_phrase\":\"unavailable\",\"source_span\":\"unavailable\",\"source_sentence\":\"During those hours, apps covered by the plan would be unavailable by default.\",\"ja_gloss\":\"利用できない\",\"phrase_type\":\"word\",\"normalization_type\":\"none\",\"normalization_note\":\"形容詞の原形をそのまま使用。\",\"selection_reason\":\"深夜にアプリがどうなるのかを直接示す一般語で、計画の基本動作の理解に不可欠。\",\"listening_difficulty_reason\":\"音節が多いうえ、否定を担う接頭辞un-を聞き逃すと意味が逆になる。\",\"inference_transparency\":\"HIGH\",\"topic_exposure_dependency\":\"LOW\",\"comprehension_impact\":\"HIGH\",\"figurative_or_emotional_value\":\"LOW\",\"spoiler_risk\":\"LOW\",\"portfolio_category\":\"general_unknown_word\",\"portfolio_substitution\":false,\"portfolio_substitution_reason\":\"該当なし。各カテゴリから2件ずつ選定。\"},{\"rank\":7,\"display_phrase\":\"depend on\",\"source_span\":\"depend on\",\"source_sentence\":\"Its success will not depend on how many teenagers change the setting.\",\"ja_gloss\":\"～次第である\",\"phrase_type\":\"phrasal_verb\",\"normalization_type\":\"none\",\"normalization_note\":\"本文ですでに基本形。\",\"selection_reason\":\"最終段落で、計画の成功を判断する条件が何かを示す因果・条件表現。\",\"listening_difficulty_reason\":\"depend onが後続する長い疑問節と連続するため、何が何に左右されるのかを保持しにくい。\",\"inference_transparency\":\"HIGH\",\"topic_exposure_dependency\":\"LOW\",\"comprehension_impact\":\"HIGH\",\"figurative_or_emotional_value\":\"LOW\",\"spoiler_risk\":\"LOW\",\"portfolio_category\":\"causal_contrast\",\"portfolio_substitution\":false,\"portfolio_substitution_reason\":\"該当なし。各カテゴリから2件ずつ選定。\"},{\"rank\":8,\"display_phrase\":\"urge\",\"source_span\":\"urge\",\"source_sentence\":\"In other words, the plan puts a small speed bump before the automatic urge to watch “just one more.”\",\"ja_gloss\":\"衝動\",\"phrase_type\":\"word\",\"normalization_type\":\"none\",\"normalization_note\":\"本文の名詞形をそのまま使用。\",\"selection_reason\":\"利用者が自動的に動画を見続ける心理を表し、設定が行動に作用する理由を理解させる。\",\"listening_difficulty_reason\":\"短く発音され、日本語話者には母音と語末子音が識別しづらい。\",\"inference_transparency\":\"MEDIUM\",\"topic_exposure_dependency\":\"LOW\",\"comprehension_impact\":\"MEDIUM\",\"figurative_or_emotional_value\":\"HIGH\",\"spoiler_risk\":\"LOW\",\"portfolio_category\":\"general_unknown_word\",\"portfolio_substitution\":false,\"portfolio_substitution_reason\":\"該当なし。各カテゴリから2件ずつ選定。\"},{\"rank\":9,\"display_phrase\":\"somewhere between\",\"source_span\":\"somewhere between\",\"source_sentence\":\"This midnight speed bump sits somewhere between a strict ban and a complete hands-off approach.\",\"ja_gloss\":\"～と～の中間に\",\"phrase_type\":\"collocation\",\"normalization_type\":\"none\",\"normalization_note\":\"二つの選択肢の中間を示す比較表現を抽出。\",\"selection_reason\":\"この計画が全面禁止でも完全放任でもないという、結論部の対比構造を示す。\",\"listening_difficulty_reason\":\"betweenの後に二つの長い名詞句が続き、対比の両端を音声上で対応させる必要がある。\",\"inference_transparency\":\"HIGH\",\"topic_exposure_dependency\":\"LOW\",\"comprehension_impact\":\"HIGH\",\"figurative_or_emotional_value\":\"MEDIUM\",\"spoiler_risk\":\"LOW\",\"portfolio_category\":\"causal_contrast\",\"portfolio_substitution\":false,\"portfolio_substitution_reason\":\"該当なし。各カテゴリから2件ずつ選定。\"},{\"rank\":10,\"display_phrase\":\"endless current of scrolling\",\"source_span\":\"endless current of scrolling\",\"source_sentence\":\"“What the UK is trying to switch off is not the glow of the smartphone, but the endless current of scrolling that carries teenagers right up to bedtime.”\",\"ja_gloss\":\"延々と続くスクロールの流れ\",\"phrase_type\":\"noun_phrase\",\"normalization_type\":\"none\",\"normalization_note\":\"引用文から水流の比喩を担う最小の名詞句を抽出。\",\"selection_reason\":\"スクロールが利用者を就寝時刻まで運ぶという、記事の主題を印象づける比喩表現。\",\"listening_difficulty_reason\":\"currentを「現在の」と解釈しやすく、ここでは止めにくい水流の比喩だと判断する必要がある。\",\"inference_transparency\":\"MEDIUM\",\"topic_exposure_dependency\":\"LOW\",\"comprehension_impact\":\"MEDIUM\",\"figurative_or_emotional_value\":\"HIGH\",\"spoiler_risk\":\"LOW\",\"portfolio_category\":\"figurative_emotional\",\"portfolio_substitution\":false,\"portfolio_substitution_reaso